#In their spare time, classmates Vasya and Petya love to play various logic games: 
#Battleship, Tic-Tac-Toe, Chess, Checkers, and many others. 
#The boys have already tried and played all sorts of classic games of this kind, 
#including computer ones. One day, they wanted to play something new, 
#but couldn't find anything suitable.
#So, Petya came up with the following game, "Guessing":
#There are two players. The first player thinks of any three-digit number, 
#such that the first and last digits differ from each other by more than one. 
#Next, the player who thought of the number reverses it by swapping the first and last digits, 
#thereby obtaining another number. Then, the smaller of the two numbers is subtracted from the larger one.
#The second player's task is to guess the resulting number based on its first digit. 
#For example, if Vasya thought of the number 487, then by rearranging the first and last digits, he gets the number 784. 
#After that, he has to subtract 487 from 784, resulting in the number 297. 
#Petya must guess this result using the provided first digit, which is 2.
#Petya is better at math than Vasya, so he almost always wins games of this type. 
#However, in this case, Petya cheated and specifically invented a game that has a winning strategy, 
#ensuring he won't lose to Vasya under any circumstances.
#The Winning Strategy:
#The result of the subtraction is always a three-digit number, its second digit is always 9, 
#and to get the value of the last digit, it is sufficient to subtract the first digit from 9. 
#In the case discussed above, the last digit is 9 - 2 = 7.
#Help Petya further simplify the process of guessing the number by writing a program for it.
#Input Data
#The single line of the input file INPUT.TXT contains a single digit K, corresponding to the first digit of the number obtained by Vasya.
#Output Data
#In the output file OUTPUT.TXT, you need to output the full value of the difference obtained by Vasya.


k = int(input()) 
second = 9
third = 9 - k

print(f"{k}{second}{third}")
